So, 2/5 of 200. Let me compute that. 200 divided by 5 is 40, and then multiplied by 2 gives 80. So there are 80 boys. That makes sense. Then the rest are girls. So total students minus number of boys would be the number of girls. So 200 - 80 is 120 girls. Okay, that seems straightforward.

